{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated code generation pipeline (cobbler orchestrator) and has assigned task #5644: implement cmd/stty features for srd105-stty requirements R2.1, R3.1, R3.2, and R4.1. The task extends an existing stty implementation that currently only supports R1.1 (default display with no arguments). The specific requirements are:\n   - **R2.1**: `-a` or `--all` must print all current terminal settings in human-readable format\n   - **R3.1**: `-g` or `--save` must print machine-readable format that can be fed back to restore settings\n   - **R3.2**: `-F DEVICE` or `--file=DEVICE` must operate on specified terminal device instead of stdin\n   - **R4.1**: Accept setting names as arguments to enable them, and names prefixed with `-` to disable them (e.g., `stty -echo` disables echo, `stty echo` enables it)\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: code compiles (`go build`), tests pass (`go test`), `go vet` clean, each requirement has at least one differential test case.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing**: Tests compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gstty`) using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **termios**: Terminal I/O settings via `golang.org/x/sys/unix` - `unix.IoctlGetTermios`, `unix.IoctlSetTermios`, `unix.TIOCGETA`, `unix.TIOCSETA`\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` must be called at start of main\n   - **Flag definitions**: `flagDef` struct with name, mask, sane default; organized into iflags, oflags, cflags, lflags arrays\n   - **Control characters**: `ccDef` struct with name, index, saneVal, isNum; array of 18 control chars\n   - **Window size**: `unix.IoctlGetWinsize` with `unix.TIOCGWINSZ`\n   - **vdisable**: `0xff` con