{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019mhqP73ZquCVo2Eb2hfoPb","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my thorough search, let me provide you with what I found:\n\n## Summary of GNU stty -a and -g Output Format References\n\nI've searched through the repository comprehensively. Here's what I found:\n\n### Current Implementation Status\n\n**File: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5644/cmd/stty/main.go`**\n\nThe current implementation (243 lines) shows:\n- Only the default display mode is implemented (no arguments)\n- The `-a` and `-g` flags are mentioned in the help text but are **not yet implemented**\n- The code parses arguments but rejects anything except `--help` and `--version`\n\n### What the Specification Requires\n\n**From `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5644/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd105-stty.yaml`:**\n\n- **R2.1 (-a flag)**: \"-a or --all must print all current terminal settings in a **human-readable format**.\"\n- **R3.1 (-g flag)**: \"-g or --save must print all current terminal settings in a **machine-readable format (stty-readable)** that can be passed back as arguments to restore settings.\"\n\n### Default Display Format (Currently Implemented)\n\nThe `speedLine()` function (lines 181-186) shows the output format for the default display:\n```\nspeed <N> baud; rows <rows>; columns <cols>;\n```\n\nor if input and output speeds differ:\n```\nispeed <N> baud; ospeed <N> baud; rows <rows>; columns <cols>;\n```\n\n### Available Constants and Mappings\n\nThe code defines **baud rate handling** indirectly through `unix.Termios`:\n- `t.Ispeed` - input speed (stored as numeric baud rate value)\n- `t.Ospeed` - output speed (stored as numeric baud rate value)\n\nHowever, **no baud rate constant mappings** (B9600, B4800, etc.) are present in the current code. These would need to be created for the `-g` output format.\n\n### Flag and Control Character Definitions\n\nThe code has comprehensive constants for:\n- **Input flags** (iflags, 13 flags): ignbrk, brkint, ignpar, parmrk, inpck, istrip, inlcr, igncr, icrnl, ixon, ixoff, ixany, imaxbel\n- **Output flags** (oflags, 5 flags): opost, onlcr, ocrnl, onocr, onlret\n- **Control flags** (cflags, 6 flags): cstopb, cread, parenb, parodd, hupcl, clocal\n- **Local flags** (lflags, 13 flags): isig, icanon, echo, echoe, echok, echonl, noflsh, tostop, echoctl, echoprt, echoke, flusho, pendin, iexten\n- **Control characters** (18 chars): intr, quit, erase, kill, eof, eol, eol2, start, stop, susp, dsusp, reprint, werase, lnext, discard, status, min, time\n\n### Missing Implementations\n\nThe `-a` and `-g` flag handlers are **not yet implemented** in the parseArgs function. The test suite (test-rel15.0.yaml) shows placeholder tests with empty stdout expectations, indicating these features need to be built."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"134b6010-6885-4f08-8e6f-190349c7e60e","uuid":"42b4544a-5e50-4980-a44f-d19d7412d6cc","timestamp":"2026-05-29T15:31:03.691Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5644, look for any reference to the GNU stty -a output format — check docs/, any .yaml files, or comments in existing stty code that show what the -a output should look like. Also check if there are speed/baud rate constant mappings anywhere (like a map from baud rate integers to B9600-style constants). I want to understand what format -a and -g should output.","agentId":"ad5720ba086d6981a","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my thorough search, let me provide you with what I found:\n\n## Summary of GNU stty -a and -g Output Format References\n\nI've searched through the repository comprehensively. Here's what I found:\n\n### Current Implementation Status\n\n**File: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zk